<p>My name is Sheldon Kotyk.</p>
<p>I am the Digital Engineer and Strategist at <a href="https://p2c.com">Power to Change</a>. I sit on our Digital Task Force with senior leaders from operations and IT, where we plan how the ministry uses technology, including where AI can help most and how to use it safely. I also lead the development team, and on each project I do both the planning and the building: creating new sites like <a target="_blank" href="https://prayforawin.com">Pray for a Win</a>, figuring out what our existing sites need, updating them and keeping them secure, and building new apps. Today&#039;s tools let us build and test ideas quickly, so we can take on work we didn&#039;t have the capacity for before. For my ministry updates, check <a href="https://kotyk.com/blog">my blog</a>.</p>
<p>I married my <a href="http://juliekotyk.com">best friend Julie</a> and we have three daughters; Kristin, Ava and Jamie. We have a <a href="/boston">dog named Boston</a> and also have two cats; Popcorn and <a href="https://www.instagram.com/theodorecorneliusfeles/">Theodore Cornelious</a>. Unfortunately Candycorn recently passed away.</p>
<p>In my free time, I build web sites and applications under the name <a href="https://abigah.com">Abigah</a>. <a href="/abigah">Why is it called Abigah?</a>. How did I learn how to build websites? <a href="https://kotyk.com/about/how-do-i-learn-the-technical">I&#039;m glad you asked</a>.</p>
<p>If you want to know the details behind Kotyk.com, check out the <a href="/about/colophon">colophon</a>.</p>
